          <p style="margin:0;padding:0 44px 22px 2px;font-size:15px;line-height:24px">No. Bring what you have, whether that is inspiration, a rough idea, or existing documents. The first conversation should help clarify what information is needed to move forward thoughtfully.</p>
        </details>
        <details style="border-bottom:1px solid #B5BCC0">
          <summary style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:18px;padding:20px 2px;cursor:pointer;font-family:'Noto Serif',Georgia,serif;font-size:18px;line-height:26px;color:#5D5D5D">
            <span style="flex:1">Will my home addition need permits?</span>
            <span class="faq-plus" style="flex:0 0 auto;font-family:Lato,sans-serif;font-size:22px;color:#7A3F96;transition:transform 200ms cubic-bezier(.25,.1,.25,1)">+</span>
          </summary>
          <p style="margin:0;padding:0 44px 22px 2px;font-size:15px;line-height:24px">Additions generally require permits. LA County specifically lists additions among work that generally requires a permit, while the City of Los Angeles explains that the review path can depend on complexity and scope.</p>
        </details>
      </div>
      <div style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;border-top:1px solid #B5BCC0">
        <details style="border-bottom:1px solid #B5BCC0">
          <summary style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:18px;padding:20px 2px;cursor:pointer;font-family:'Noto Serif',Georgia,serif;font-size:18px;line-height:26px;color:#5D5D5D">
